══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
4. BOTTOM LINE
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

No single option is best on every dimension.
The decision hinges on three questions:

  1. How important is cost efficiency at scale?
     → ECS/EC2 Multitenant wins clearly above 9 tenants.

  2. How much infra management capacity does the team have?
     → Low capacity favours Fargate or Cosmos.

  3. Are there regulatory requirements for dedicated tenant infrastructure?
     → Single-tenant EC2 is the safest choice.

HYBRID OPTION (recommended if priorities differ across tenants):
  • Standard tenants       → ECS/EC2 Multitenant  (cost-efficient)
  • High-compliance tenants→ ECS/EC2 Single-tenant (dedicated infra)
  • Burst / new onboarding → Fargate or Cosmos     (fast, zero setup)

